description_text:
Overview
Are you a passionate problem solver, equally comfortable thinking outside the box while successfully delivering within present constraints? Do you love working with bleeding-edge technology and influencing the direction of a platform used by over 100 million people? Are you driven by integrity and obsessed with process efficiency? We have a rare opportunity to grow our in-house eDiscovery team, managing the technical aspects of discovery for a very active and dynamic docket. You’ll have close contact with the product teams developing features designed to revolutionize corporate eDiscovery processes, and get to work with new datatypes in an ever-evolving and diverse technical environment. We need someone who enthusiastically leans into new challenges, approaching each with a fresh, learn-it-all perspective. You are comfortable in a state of flux, with an unwavering commitment toward delivering the right outcome every time. We need an eDiscovery professional who is skilled in concepts underlying the common tools, not just a good operator of the industry standards. Action-oriented creativity is valued. If that sounds like you, we can’t wait to meet you!

Responsibilities
- Partner with outside counsel and review hosting vendors to ensure the end-to-end eDiscovery processes for assigned matters flow as defensibly, consistently, and efficiently as possible.- Identify, extract, and classify required review sets using complex query filters, analytics, and AI;
- Remediate corrupt, encrypted, or otherwise inaccessible content;
- Maintain detailed tracking logs and statistics regarding throughput.

- Continuously maintain evergreen processes as platform technology evolves. Proactively ascertain weak points and devise solutions. Identify and disseminate updates and workarounds across the team so discovery obligations can ultimately be met.
- Manage data retention operations and processes, from a platform level to individual workflows.
- Partner with the Microsoft Purview team and other product groups on eDiscovery requirements. Provide detailed voice-of-the-customer usage scenarios and feedback, identifying product blocking issues, workarounds, and opportunities to improve. Strategically conceive and execute critical test passes and comprehensively document results.
- Partner with Engineering to drive custom development and infrastructural build-out.
- Evangelize and showcase Purview eDiscovery capabilities via direct customer engagements and industry events.

Qualifications
Required Qualifications:
- Master's Degree in Business, Project Management, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, Engineering, or related field AND 3+ years experience in project management, operations, or engineering- OR Bachelor's Degree in Business, Project Management, Supply Chain, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, Engineering, or related field AND 4+ years experience in project management, operations, or engineering
- OR equivalent experience. 

Preferred Qualifications:
- Minimum 10 years of direct System Administrator experience with common eDiscovery tools (e.g., Relativity, Nuix, Brainspace, etc.);
- RCA certification;
- Direct experience with the Relativity aiR suite and/or other GenAI capabilities for document review;
- Experience with process automation and scripting languages – e.g., PowerShell, SQL, Python;
- Demonstrated ability to devise reliable solutions within the limitations of the available technology platforms in your toolset;
- Firsthand experience, or at least conversant familiarity, with the eDiscovery and Compliance capabilities in M365/Purview;
- In-depth familiarity with the litigation support ecosystem, tools, and vendors;
- Proven analytical and technical skills;
- Meticulous attention to detail and proven organizational skills;
- Ability to work independently on multiple projects with minimal supervision in a fast-paced environment, and able to manage and prioritize multiple deadlines;
- Microsoft platform proficiency – especially Exchange, SharePoint, Teams, and Azure.


Technical Solution Management IC4 - The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is USD $96,500 - $188,400 per year. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations, within the San Francisco Bay area and New York City metropolitan area, and the base pay range for this role in those locations is USD $123,500 - $206,400 per year. 

 Certain roles may be eligible for benefits and other compensation. Find additional benefits and pay information here:
https://careers.microsoft.com/us/en/us-corporate-pay

This position will be open for a minimum of 5 days, with applications accepted on an ongoing basis until the position is filled.

Microsoft is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, citizenship, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, immigration status, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran or military status, race, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance with religious accommodations and/or a reasonable accommodation due to a disability during the application process, read more about requesting accommodations.
